1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,361
This is Talang,
a sealed-bid repo desk on Canton.

2
00:00:04,911 --> 00:00:08,726
Repo is how bond holders
raise cash without selling.

3
00:00:08,726 --> 00:00:13,197
But asking five lenders for a price
tells all five you need money.

4
00:00:13,747 --> 00:00:17,366
On Talang, a quote goes
to the borrower alone.

5
00:00:17,366 --> 00:00:20,218
Canton never sends it to a rival's node.

6
00:00:20,768 --> 00:00:23,295
Here's the desk, typed in live.

7
00:00:23,295 --> 00:00:29,097
The borrower asks for five point three
million USDC against sixty Treasury notes.

8
00:00:29,097 --> 00:00:32,345
It asks three lenders, Lender C included.

9
00:00:32,895 --> 00:00:36,039
Lender A types its rate and haircut,

10
00:00:36,039 --> 00:00:39,079
and seals the quote,
with the cash locked behind it.

11
00:00:39,079 --> 00:00:41,629
Its node shows only its own quotes.

12
00:00:42,179 --> 00:00:46,637
Lender B quotes the lowest rate,
but asks a six percent haircut.

13
00:00:47,187 --> 00:00:52,039
Lender C types four ninety-five,
with a three percent haircut.

14
00:00:53,627 --> 00:00:58,969
The borrower sees three sealed quotes.
Lender B's is short at the mark.

15
00:00:58,969 --> 00:01:02,232
So it takes the cheapest
quote that covers.

16
00:01:02,232 --> 00:01:05,782
Cash and collateral
move in one transaction.

17
00:01:06,332 --> 00:01:09,422
Lender B learns its rank,
and nothing else.

18
00:01:11,052 --> 00:01:14,197
The regulator sees best execution:

19
00:01:14,197 --> 00:01:17,826
the winner ranked second on rate,
and no lender is named.

20
00:01:18,376 --> 00:01:23,176
Side by side, every node
reads only its own ledger.

21
00:01:23,726 --> 00:01:28,526
Then the valuation agent types a lower
mark for the notes, and publishes it.

22
00:01:29,326 --> 00:01:34,165
At that mark, Lender A's repo
is short, so it calls margin.

23
00:01:35,166 --> 00:01:39,416
But one agent shouldn't set
the mark alone. So a committee does.

24
00:01:39,416 --> 00:01:43,745
It's one decentralized
party on three Canton nodes,

25
00:01:43,745 --> 00:01:47,126
run through BitSafe's
Decentralization Manager.

26
00:01:47,126 --> 00:01:49,137
Two of three must confirm.

27
00:01:49,687 --> 00:01:54,961
Node one proposes a markdown,
as a BitSafe governable action.

28
00:01:55,511 --> 00:02:00,811
It confirms. But one confirmation
isn't enough, so nothing is published.

29
00:02:01,361 --> 00:02:06,805
Node two, in its own DecMan,
confirms. Now the threshold is met.

30
00:02:07,355 --> 00:02:10,774
Execute, and the mark
is published as the committee.

31
00:02:11,579 --> 00:02:16,235
Node three didn't vote,
but its audit trail shows every step.

32
00:02:18,043 --> 00:02:22,764
The lender calls margin with that mark.
No single pricer could have moved it.

33
00:02:23,314 --> 00:02:25,314
With one of three nodes stopped,

34
00:02:25,314 --> 00:02:28,841
the committee still published.
With two stopped, it couldn't.

35
00:02:28,841 --> 00:02:34,470
That was on a DecMan LocalNet. On DevNet,
it's still waiting on rights from NODERS.

36
00:02:35,020 --> 00:02:39,743
Both legs can be real tokens.
On the NODERS DevNet participant,

37
00:02:39,743 --> 00:02:44,585
a repo ran with Canton Coin
as cash and CBTC as collateral,

38
00:02:44,585 --> 00:02:47,967
each allocated through its registry.

39
00:02:47,967 --> 00:02:53,664
At repurchase, the Canton Coin went
to the lender and the CBTC went home.

40
00:02:53,664 --> 00:02:56,096
Every step has an update ID.

41
00:02:56,646 --> 00:03:01,817
With Grofty, the wallet's key
authorizes each desk command,

42
00:03:01,817 --> 00:03:05,356
by signing a one-time
challenge with CIP-0103.

43
00:03:05,356 --> 00:03:09,617
It's tested with a stub wallet,
but not yet with a live Grofty wallet.

44
00:03:10,167 --> 00:03:14,154
Each desk can also have
an AI agent, over MCP.

45
00:03:14,154 --> 00:03:16,614
It reads only its own party's node.

46
00:03:16,614 --> 00:03:20,099
A lender's agent never
sees a rival's rate.

47
00:03:20,649 --> 00:03:25,149
The business is a venue fee,
in basis points on the principal.

48
00:03:25,149 --> 00:03:28,833
It's collected inside
every repurchase and roll,

49
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:32,725
so it can't be skipped.
It's built, with no revenue yet.

50
00:03:33,275 --> 00:03:38,854
Next: a two-week shadow book on DevNet,
then small live repos on MainNet.

51
00:03:38,854 --> 00:03:46,272
Not done yet: the committee on DevNet,
USDCx, a live wallet, and any pilot user.

52
00:03:46,822 --> 00:03:51,335
That's Talang. The desk
is at talang-desk.vercel.app.

53
00:03:51,335 --> 00:03:56,783
The code is at
github.com/PugarHuda/talang.

